// The residue: a type parameter **no channel** delivers is still E0058, with the tailored message
// that says which channel is missing and how to get one.
//
// Forwarding the turbofish arm did not make the diagnostic go away, it narrowed it to the cases
// where it is still true. Both survivors are bodies a per-call channel cannot reach:
//
//   * a nested `fn` inside an INSTANCE method of a generic type — the class's `T` rides the
//     receiver's tag, and a nested `fn` has no receiver (it carries no hidden slots of its own
//     either, D2b);
//   * a nested `fn`'s OWN `<U>` — it is not a declared top-level generic, so no call site fills a
//     slot for it and nothing names its instantiation.
//
// `type_name::<T>()` fails in exactly these places for exactly this reason, which is why the help no
// longer says "pass the name instead of the type": the composed route is shut here too. Pinned so a
// future help-text edit cannot reintroduce advice that does not work.
//
// The third line is the STATIC arm's other guarantee, unchanged: a turbofish naming a type that
// resolves to nothing stays E0013. Forwarding a parameter must never turn a typo into a silent
// empty list — that leniency belongs to the dynamic arm alone.
// expect: error E0058 at 35:51
// expect: error E0058 at 43:47
// expect: error E0013 at 47:43
// expect: exit 1
struct Todo {
    id: int
    title: string
}

class Repo<T> {
    pub tbl: string

    fn new(tbl: string): Repo<T> { return Repo { tbl: tbl }; }

    fn nested(): int {
        fn inner(): int { return field_specs_of::<T>().len() }
        if self.tbl == "" { return 0 }
        return inner();
    }
}

fn outer<T>(): int {
    // The enclosing `T` forwards; this nested declaration's own `U` has no call site to fill it.
    fn inner<U>(): int { return variants_of::<U>().len() }
    return inner() + field_specs_of::<T>().len();
}

fn bogus(): int { return field_specs_of::<NoSuchType>().len() }
